{
  "requirement": "The `requirement` string in each evidence file MUST match all Markdown inside its fenced `{req}` directive, excluding leading and trailing whitespace. Habeas MUST report changed requirement text.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations**\n1. The `requirement` string in each evidence file MUST match all Markdown inside its fenced `{req}` directive. Leading and trailing whitespace are excluded.\n2. Habeas MUST report changed requirement text.\n\n**Code**\n- **Declared text:** `collect_definitions` in `src/evidence.rs` builds the declared text. It takes the whole directive body (`body_start..body_end`) through `crate::without_options(...)` and then `.trim()`, so leading and trailing whitespace are excluded.\n- **Option lines:** `without_options` in `src/lib.rs` is marked `{impl}` for this requirement. It removes the `:impl:` and `:test:` option lines, which are metadata and not body Markdown.\n- **Comparison and report:** `validate_evidence_file` in `src/evidence.rs` is marked `{impl}`. It compares the evidence string with `expected.text`. On a mismatch it pushes a \"`<field> text changed (<source>)`\" error with a compact `-`/`+` diff. The recorded text is also checked for being nonempty.\n- **Example evidence:** the same code handles example evidence through `kind.noun()`.\n\n**Marking**\n- The body-extraction and trim step in `collect_definitions` carries `{impl}` for `requirements.ci.span` and `requirements.references.anchors`, not for `requirements.ci.requirement_text`.\n- `ci.span` states the same body rule, including \"Leading and trailing whitespace MUST be excluded when comparing the body with evidence\". I judge that marking acceptable and do not count it as a gap.\n- I found no other unmarked code implementing this requirement.\n\n**Tests**\n- `validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` (`{test}` marked) uses a body with a nested code fence containing a `{req}` role. The evidence text matches the trimmed body and validation reports no errors.\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` (`{test}` marked) records stale text (\"Old text.\") against \"First.\" and asserts \"requirement text changed\", \"- Old text.\" and \"+ First.\". It also asserts \"requirement must be a string\" for a non-string value.\n- `anchored_files_must_be_completely_covered_and_resolvable` (`{test}` marked) checks that option lines are excluded from the compared text, by asserting no \"text changed\" error.\n- All three tests run with fixture bodies that include surrounding newlines, which the trim removes. Together they cover both the match and the changed-text report.\n\nI found no unspecified behavior and no unacknowledged gaps.",
  "references": "c0914c5fe4c4c712a6a8d74e9672f3c5fb2d82ee145425de57b43b1fd02361fc",
